# Leap of Void — Project Overview

One-touch endless mobile game: a ball orbits a planet, tap to release along the
orbit tangent, graze the next planet to get captured into its orbit. Chain hops
forever, score-based, deaths are dramatic. iOS first via Expo/EAS, Android later.

**`orbit-game-plan.md` at the repo root is the design source of truth.** All core
decisions there are settled — do not re-litigate them. If a task seems to require
changing a settled decision, ask the user first.

## Non-negotiable constraints

- **Portrait, locked, designed for 9:16.** Every visual must read in a tiny muted
  vertical TikTok clip. "Does this make a better 5–15 second clip?" is the design test.
- **One-touch input only.** Single tap anywhere = release. No gestures, no buttons in gameplay.
- **No physics engine.** Everything is circle math + line geometry. Deterministic, tunable.
- **Instant play.** No tutorial, no sign-up, restart in under 1 second after death.
- **Ship fast.** Prefer the simplest implementation that feels good. Polish comes in
  the dedicated juice pass (Milestone 3), not opportunistically.

## Scope guard — do NOT build (v2 parking lot)

Orbit-radius-from-graze-distance, black hole chase, skins/trails, daily challenge,
leaderboards, ads code. Death flow should leave room for a future "continue" slot,
but no ad SDK in v1.

## Roadmap position

Track milestone progress here as milestones complete:

- [x] M1: Core loop prototype (static planet chain, orbit, tap-release, capture/crash/miss, death, restart, score) — feel validated on device
- [x] M2: Procedural generation, camera follow, difficulty dials, orbit decay — implemented; difficulty numbers still being tuned on device
- [ ] M3: Juice pass (trail, particles, shake, haptics, SFX, combo/graze/perfect, zones)
- [ ] M4: Meta screens (home, death card, settings, best-score persistence)
- [ ] M5: Ship (icon, branding, EAS build, TestFlight, App Store)
